\id GEN  
\h Genesis 
\toc1 GENESIS 
\toc2 Genesis 
\toc3 GEN 
\mt1 GENESIS  
\c 47  
\p
\v 1 And Joseph came and told Pharao, \add saying\add*, My father, and my brethren, and their cattle, and their oxen, and all their possessions, are come out of the land of Chanaan, and behold, they are in the land of Gesem.  
\v 2 And he took of his brethren five men, and set them before Pharao.  
\v 3 And Pharao said to the brethren of Joseph, What is your occupation? and they said to Pharao, Your servants are shepherds, both we and our father.  
\v 4 And they said to Pharao, We are come to sojourn in the land, for there is no pasture for the flocks of your servants, for the famine has prevailed in the land of Chanaan; now then, \f + \fr 47:4 \ft Or, let us dwell. See 1 Tim 6:8. \f* we will dwell in the land of Gesem. And Pharao said to Joseph, Let them dwell in the land of Gesem; and if you know that there are among them able men, make them overseers of my cattle. So Jacob and his sons came into Egypt, to Joseph; and Pharao, king of Egypt, heard \add of it\add*.  
\v 5 And Pharao spoke to Joseph, saying, Your father, and your brethren, are come to you.  
\v 6 Behold, the land of Egypt is before you; settle your father and your brethren in the best land.  
